hey there townscaper so i was asked a  really interesting question someone  asked me how do you zoom into  really tall buildings and i can see why  they were asked that because if you're  just getting into the game and you play  something else the controls can be  a little wonky they could be a little  intimidating a perfect example of this  would be the sims 4. the controls are  literally inverted so it makes for some  really interesting first time gameplay  you want to rotate your camera but you  end up panning it like this or you want  to pan your camera but you end up  rotating  it like this so yeah i'm going to keep  this short as possible i'm going to go  over the camera controls and then we'll  get into the zooming part so obviously  to zoom in and out you want to use the  middle scroll button  if you want to rotate your camera you  want to take your left click button  and you want to just drag it this is me  rotating to the left just me rotating to  the right  of course you pull your mouse down while  you're holding the left click if you  want a bird's eye view  and if you want a full frontal view you  just go on ahead and push your mouse  upwards so if you want to pin  you want to hold your right click button  this is me panning to the left this is  me panning to the right  and if you want to move it upwards you  just drag it up  if you want to move it down you just  move it down so to get started  let's just start from all the way in the  back if you zoom the camera all the way  in the back  and you pan your camera to the bottom  and you zoom in you'll notice that  you'll go all the way to the base of  your build  this is about the fourth story third and  fourth story so if you want to get to  the middle all you have to do of course  is pan your camera using the right click  button so i'm taking my right click  button and i'm dragging the camera  upwards i just took my left click button  so that i can rotate and adjust to  center view  and now i'm at about the 10th story if  i'm not mistaken one two three four five  six  seven eight nine ten is the tenth story  if you want to go even further  of course all you have to do is take  your right click button  and drag the camera upwards of course  you're gonna take your left click and  you're gonna  adjust it and now you're at the top of  the building now this  is a pretty simple example because  um this building is actually pretty  short this is about  20 20 stories i have an example right  here  um i believe it's about 60 stories  please don't quote me because i count it  like three times and so this is it right  here  and just going to show you that example  again i'm zooming all the way out  i've pinned my camera to the bottom so  as soon as you zoom in it's going to  take you right to the base of the build  this is the third story  uh and of course if you zoom out and you  panned up  at this point the building's so tall  that you're basically scaling it to get  to the top you can zoom out  and now you're basically your camera's  at center  point if you will and you zoom in and  you're right at the middle of it you  take your left click button and you  center it if you want to get all the way  to the top for a building like this  i highly recommend that you just zoom  all the way out take your right click  button  pan it as far as you can like you see  how i'm scaling all the way to the top i  can't even pull the mouse down anymore  and then zoom in and boom there you have  it uh take the left click button to  rotate so you can see what you have  going on  and you can take it to bird's eye view  thing about bird's eye view  in tall buildings is that of course with  any building you're going to hit the top  you're going to hit the roof but once  you zoom out it'll only go so far  until of course you increase the size of  the building  and then the camera will adjust so what  i noticed about this  it's perfect because it it can work out  to make for some  really nice pictures if you practice it  zoom in pretty well i'll show you an  example right here like try to get to  this staircase  so wasd those help you go forward back  left right you want to get in as  as close as possible so i'm just going  to go through the controls as i do this  right now i'm using the right click  button to pan the camera  i can't zoom in anymore i've literally  zoomed in as much as i could so i'm  going to take the left click button i'm  going to take the left click  and i'm going to drag it  and try to get in as much as possible i  just use the  w key or the up key i'm still using the  left click  now i'm using the right click to pull  pull it i'm adjusting  i'm moving in a little further with the  directional button  now you can kind of see the the  staircase right here but you still need  a little bit of adjusting so i'm right  clicking i'm pulling it back  then i take the left click button i kind  of tilt it  i'm pushing the w key or you can use the  up key to get me closer  i'm left clicking and i'm panning the  camera  while rotating the camera downwards if  you will and now i'm panning as close as  i possibly can  this is as close as we can get this is  me pushing w  um now i'm pushing s to go backwards so  yeah this makes for really really great  up close pictures  so take that in and make some really  great townscaper photos  so that's it for today if this video  helped you out please make sure that you  like and share to help me out if you  haven't subscribed go ahead and hit that  button it'll help me out as well and i  really appreciate the support you guys  if you haven't seen my two series the  random clicking series or the connecting  small town  series please check those out they  should pop up in the cards in the top  right corner of the video here  but anyways i just want to thank you  guys so much for viewing um it's greatly  appreciated  please make sure that you check out my  content make sure that you like  subscribe and comment  